    <briefdescription>
<para>Functions used to compose logical expressions in tests. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The functions <computeroutput>mt::both()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>mt::either()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>mt::negate()</computeroutput> combine multiple conditions, allowing expressive and concise test logic. <computeroutput>mt::either()</computeroutput> is an inclusive or: it is true also when both conditions are true.</para>
<para>The functions have descriptive names, since <computeroutput>and</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>or</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>not</computeroutput> are alternative tokens and cannot be used as identifiers. Using these logical functions allows developers to express compound conditions clearly and improve readability.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>compound<sp/>conditions&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::both<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>mt::eq<sp/>(compute_float<sp/>(),<sp/>42.0)));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>When operands are function comparators, use the overloaded logical operators <computeroutput>&amp;&amp;</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>||</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>!</computeroutput> provided in the <computeroutput>micro_test_plus::operators</computeroutput> namespace for more natural logical expressions.  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
